{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/3q5ojqpg","slide":8,"text":"The configured secret loads before auth initialization, so reloads do not invalidate active tokens.","textPreview":"The configured secret loads before auth initialization, so reloads do not invalidate active tokens.","textChars":99,"textLines":1,"bbox":[646,440,420,42]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/cn1ei9","slide":8,"text":"Presenter 3\n\nA financial workspace must keep data scoped correctly. Clarafin protects API routes with JWT access tokens and filters documents and analyses by the authenticated user. We also resolved a reload issue by loading the configured signing key before authentication initializes, so valid user sessions remain stable across a backend reload.\n\n[Sources]\nProject repository: Clarafin README, frontend/src/App.jsx, backend/main.py, backend/database.py."}
